 r←{connectionParms}SendEmailExample y;emailAddress;filenames;myConnection;mailParms;rc;msg;log
⍝ Sends a test email to an email address, using your own SMTP account.\\
⍝ `⍺` must be an instance of `ConnectionParameters` with at least `Server`, `Userid` and `Password` set,
⍝ and `Port` and `Secure` if the defaults (465 and 1) are not right for your server.\\
⍝ `⍵` is either an email address, or an email address followed by one or more filenames:\\
⍝ `'john.doe@example.com'`\\
⍝ `'john.doe@example.com' 'report.pdf' 'data.csv'`\\
⍝ The files are attached to the email; relative filenames are relative to the current directory.\\
⍝ The email is sent from `Userid` (see `MailParameters.From`).\\
⍝ Returns a message that says whether the email was sent.\\
⍝ Example:\\
⍝ ```
⍝ cp←⎕NEW SMTP.ConnectionParameters
⍝ cp.(Server Userid Password)←'smtp.example.com' 'me@example.com' 'my-app-password'
⍝ cp SMTP.SendEmailExample 'john.doe@example.com'
⍝ ```
⍝ Do not put credentials into a file that is under version control.
 :If 9≠⎕NC'connectionParms'
 :OrIf ConnectionParameters≢⊃⊃⎕CLASS connectionParms
     'Left argument must be an instance of ConnectionParameters'⎕SIGNAL 11
 :EndIf
 :If 80=⎕DR y
     emailAddress←y
     filenames←''
 :Else
     emailAddress←⊃y
     filenames←⊃,/⊆¨1↓y
 :EndIf

 myConnection←⎕NEW Connection(,⊂connectionParms)

 mailParms←⎕NEW MailParameters
 mailParms.To←emailAddress
 mailParms.Subject←'Test email from APLTeam''s SMTP package'
 mailParms.Body←'This is a test email, sent by the SendEmailExample function of the SMTP package.' ⍝ Can also be a vector of text vectors

 :If 0<≢filenames
     mailParms.AddAttachment¨filenames
 :EndIf

 (rc msg log)←myConnection.Send mailParms
 :If 0=rc
     r←'Email was sent successfully'
 :Else
     r←'Failed with rc=',(⍕rc),'; ',⊃{⍺,'; ',⍵}/⊆msg
 :EndIf
